WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
[Symptoms in Schizophrenia, James D. Page, The University of Rochester]

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:12.000
[Schizophrenia (dementia praecox) is the most prevalent of mental disorders. About one per cent of the population eventually develop it.]

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:19.000
[It is essentially a chronic disease of unknown origin, characterized by marked personality disintegration.]

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:28.000
[In general appearance schizophrenics resemble normal individuals. All body types are represented. Distinction lies in their mental content and behavior.]

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:34.500
[Schizophrenics are divided into four clinical groups: simple, paranoid, catatonic and hebephrenic.]

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:43.600
[Apathy and absence of social interest characterize all types, especially the simple group who exhibit few additional symptoms.]

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.040
[Outdoor scene with some men seated on benches and some men standing.]

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:53.060
[Some men are pacing and others look disturbed.]

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.280
[Delusions and hallucinations occur in most hebephrenic, catatonic and paranoid patients.] 

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:06.620
[The latter often give evidence of these symptoms by conversing or arguing with imaginary individuals.]

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:20.000
[A woman is seated in a rocking chair on a fenced-in outdoor porch. She seems to be talking to an imaginary person.]

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:36.000
[A man is standing inside a building near a window and looking outside. He is gesticulating and seems agitated.]

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:54.000
[A woman is standing outside. She has on a floral dress and a white cloth mask over the upper part of her face, with holes cut for her eyes. She is pointing and yelling.]

00:01:54.260 --> 00:02:00.100
[Silly grinning and talking to oneself distinguish the hebephrenic.]

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:29.940
[A man is seated in a rocking chair with a blindfold over his eyes. He is laughing and talking to himself.]

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.600
[A woman is standing on the lawn outside.]

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.140
[She has on a mask with eyeholes and is wearing a floral dress. She is talking.]

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:39.240
[A man is seated in front of a brick wall. His eyes are covered by a white cloth blindfold.] 

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:46.820
[He is talking, grinning, and laughing.]

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:53.900
[Mannerisms and motor stereotypes may occur in hebephrenics but they are essentially catatonic symptoms.]

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.960
[A man is seated outside with a brick building behind him.]

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:04.160
[He wears a mask with eyeholes, over the upper portion of his face. He is moving his hands nervously and constantly.]

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:42.780
[He is talking and repeatedly puts his hand on his mouth, then drums his fingers on the back of his other hand.]

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.000
[A man wearing glasses is standing on the lawn outside.]

00:03:47.200 --> 00:04:32.060
[A brick building is behind him. He moves his hands in the same pattern repeatedly.]

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:44.800
[A man is seated in a chair outside. He moves his hands about and his fingertips flutter.]

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.480
[A woman in a plaid dress is seated in a chair on a porch.]

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:53.740
[Her face is half-covered with a white cloth with eyeholes. She moves her hands repeatedly near her face.]

00:04:53.960 --> 00:05:12.860
[Then she holds her hands up and repeatedly cups her chin and face.]

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:22.220
[Some catatonics passively permit their limbs to be molded at examiner's will. This waxy flexibility is called cerea flexibilitas.]

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:26.460
[A man dressed all in white manipulates the arms of a patient. The patient is a male wearing a mask with eyeholes.] 

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:48.160
[He allows the examiner to put his arms in any position without protest.]

00:05:48.320 --> 00:06:03.200
[The examiner continues to manipulate the patient's arms and body in numerous positions. The patient passively allows the manipulation.]

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.820
[The patient is now seated in a chair on the lawn.]

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.840
[The examiner continues to manipulate the patient, moving his arms and legs into awkward positions.]

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:19.340
[The spontaneous shift from an induced pose to a more natural position is slow and gradual.]

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.960
[Following sequence records the lowering of raised arms after 1, 5, and 30 minutes.]

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:30.760
[A man is outside and his arms have been placed over his head by an examiner.]

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:42.440
[He is filmed at 1, 5 and 30 minutes after being manipulated as he slowly lowers his arms to a more natural position.]

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:48.480
[Other catatonics are extremely rigid and negativistic. They actively resist change.]

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.960
[A man is outside with a brick wall behind him. An examiner attempts to move the man's arm.]

00:06:53.100 --> 00:07:00.000
[The man resists the movement.]

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:14.580
[The examiner also attempts to move the man's head as the man is seated outside, and the man resists.]

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:24.200
[The examiner attempts to move the man's head while the man is standing. The man resists all attempts.]

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:31.460
[Peculiar postures are assumed by some catatonics and often retained for days or months.]

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:35.980
[A man is outside standing beside a brick wall. He has a mask over his eyes. He is standing stiffly]

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.780
[The man is now facing the camera.]

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.180
[He is standing with his head bent down in front and is holding it with his hands on each side.]

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.960
[A woman is outside standing in front of a brick wall. She is wearing a floral dress and has a mask over her eyes.]

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.880
[Her arms are crossed over her chest and she is looking down. She doesn't move.]

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:53.980
[A person is seated in a chair facing away from the camera. The person is bent over with elbows on knees.]

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:57.420
[A woman in a floral dress is outside standing near a building.] 

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:01.420
[She has a mask over her eyes and her arms are at her sides. She is bent slightly at the waist and is looking down.]

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:06.820
[A man is seated in a chair outside with a brick wall behind him. He is bent at the waist and looking down.] 

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.180
[His hands are gripping the arms of the chair. He is motionless.]

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:13.220
[A man is seated in a chair outside with a brick wall behind him, wearing a mask with eyeholes.] 

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.760
[He is looking down and his arms and hands are between his legs.]

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:20.080
[ A man is seated in a chair parallel to a brick wall. He wears a mask with eyeholes.]

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.260
[His legs and feet are drawn up beneath him and he is seated slightly sideways in the chair.] 

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:28.120
[He moves restlessly and holds his head, covering his ears.]

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:37.960
[Echopraxia is a rare but striking catatonic symptom. Some inner forces appear to "compel" the patient to repeat the movements of others.]

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.560
[A man and a woman are seated outside on chairs.]

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:56.820
[The man makes movements with his hands and legs and the woman imitates him.]

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:05.760
[The woman's movements are somewhat exaggerated and she almost falls off the chair.]

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:21.040
[The woman continues to follow the man's arm and leg movements in an exaggerated style.]

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:44.560
[She tries to touch the examiner and almost falls over, so he helps her back into her chair. They continue the exercise.]

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.640
[The examiner rolls his arms in front of him and the woman copies him.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:53.700
[The man brushes his shoulder and the woman copies his movement.]

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:59.760
[The man does the same with the opposite shoulder and the woman again copies him.]

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:03.340
[The man touches his face repeatedly and the woman imitates his movements.]

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:09.520
[The man brushes his hair back with his hand and the woman imitates him again.]

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.100
[In contrast the following case is one of pseudo-echopraxia.] 

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:20.580
[Repetition is present but the performance, though spontaneous, is suggestive of voluntary imitation.]

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:23.460
[A male patient with his eyes covered by a mask is seated in a chair outside next to a brick building.] 

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.360
[An examiner is standing next to him.]

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:35.180
[The examiner makes various arm, leg, and head movements and the patient imitates him.]

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:47.460
[The patient seems to be following the movements voluntarily.]

00:10:47.700 --> 00:11:03.920
[The patient is now standing up and continues to imitate the examiner.]

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:15.220
[The examiner is now facing the patient and making more movements as the patient imitates him.]

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:20.860
[The examiner continues to make head, arm and other movements as the patient imitates him.]

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:31.000
[The examiner shakes hands with the patient as the film ends.]

